            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Puppet Leader and Death</strong><br>\nAfter his dismissal, Mussolini was rescued by German forces and installed as the head of a puppet regime in Northern Italy. As the war turned against the Axis powers, he attempted to flee but was captured and executed by Italian partisans in 1945.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Italy After Mussolini</strong><br>\nMussolini's death marked the end of Fascist rule in Italy, leading to the country's transition to a democratic republic and its alignment with Western powers during the Cold War.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Historical Evaluation</strong><br>\nMussolini's legacy is one of a controversial leader whose policies led to economic hardship, war, and the establishment of a regime that suppressed political freedom and was responsible for atrocities.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
